    "descriptor_block": "rdkit2d (217), median-imputed and standardised on train, clipped to +-10 (dmpnn_desc only)",
    "rationale": {
      "architecture": "Chemprop defaults (Yang et al. 2019) except hidden size: depth 3 (2 directed-edge updates + atom aggregation), mean readout, 2-layer FFN; hidden = FFN width = 200 instead of 300 because an epoch costs 22.8 s vs 42.2 s per CPU thread (profile.json), which halves the plan's wall time (1.2 h vs 2.1 h expected at 6 threads) and leaves room for contention; 2 epochs gave similar val MAE (1.09 vs 1.04). No hyper-parameter search (compute budget), so no selection effects on val or test beyond early stopping",
      "dropout": "p=0.1 in the FFN head only: mild regularisation and the Monte-Carlo-dropout rate; encoder dropout 0 (Chemprop default) keeps the encoder deterministic, so 10 MC passes cost one encoder pass",
      "optimisation": "Adam, MSE on train-standardised logS, batch 64, Noam schedule (2 warm-up epochs 1e-4 -> 1e-3, exponential decay to 1e-4 at epoch 50), gradient-norm clip 10",
      "early_stopping": "patience 10 epochs on validation MAE (log units, dropout off); best-epoch weights restored",
      "budget": "max 50 epochs: dmpnn 3 splits x 5 seeds + dmpnn_desc 3 splits x 3 seeds = 24 runs, estimated 1.2 h (worst case 1.3 h) with 6 single-thread workers (results/gnn/profile.json, plan_estimate)"
    }
  },
